Interactive USD edits of the points of meshes with many points, with the usd procedural cache_id and with the render delegate

The meshes of the other interactive tests are quads with 4 points. Here two 8x8 grids (81 points each) get their
points moved several times, then their points and topology changed together; one grid is removed and defined again.
The render delegate gives the points to Arnold as shared arrays pointing at the USD buffers (see
libs/render_delegate/shared_arrays.h), so each edit replaces a shared vlist, and the release callback of the
previous one runs during a later render or at teardown. The stage is re-rendered after each edit, and each render
must show the new positions and nothing at the old ones.
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive render session,
and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last procedural render is
compared against the reference image. The legacy reader doesn't delete removed prims, a known issue reported as a
warning.

author: Cyril Pichard

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
